%T A398317 96349547499566317178986735171200
%N A398317 Number of labeled 3-uniform hypergraphs on n vertices whose 2-section is a primitive strongly regular graph.
%C A398317 The 2-section of a hypergraph H is the graph with vertex set V(H), where two distinct vertices are adjacent iff they belong to a common hyperedge. Only hypergraphs whose 2-section is a primitive strongly regular graph are counted.
%C A398317 The nonzero terms through n=15 occur for n = 9, 10, 13, and 15, corresponding to primitive strongly regular 2-sections containing triangles.
%H A398317 A. E. Brouwer, <a href="https://aeb.win.tue.nl/graphs/srg/srgtab1-50.html">Parameters of strongly regular graphs</a>.
%F A398317 a(n) = Sum_G n!/|Aut(G)| * c(G), where the sum is over the isomorphism classes of primitive strongly regular graphs G on n vertices, and c(G) is the number of subsets of the triangles of G whose union of edges is E(G).
%e A398317 For n=9, the unique contributing graph is the strongly regular graph with parameters (9,4,1,2). Its six triangles are forced, and its automorphism group has order 72. Hence a(9) = 9!/72 = 5040.
%Y A398317 Cf. A076435 (strongly regular graphs).
